ey thought Arbor  E was a burglary suspect Barbara's  family says he was unarmed and just out  for a jog just bigger than life just no  young man and he just today our burry  would have celebrated his 26th birthday  instead protesters almost all wearing  masks packed in front of the courthouse  to demand justice for his death they  believe local authorities stalled the  investigation Turkish prosecutors have  laid charges related to the daring  escape of Nissan's former boss seven  people are accused of helping Carlos  gonna get out of Japan for pilots and an  airline official are charged with  illegally smuggling a migrant to flight  attendants are accused of failing to  report a crime  gone who was arrested over allegations  of financial misconduct skipped bail  while awaiting trial in Japan last year  it's believed he was smuggled out of  house arrest in an instrument case he  then flew to Istanbul then on to Beirut  Japan has no extradition treaty with  Lebanon up next marking the victories of  one war while fighting a different  historic battle  that was the sound heard across London  today the rural air forces red arrows  flew in formation over the city to mark  the 75th anniversary of VE Day on May 8  1945 Allied forces accepted Nazi  Germany's surrender bringing an end to  the Second World War in Europe similar  fly pass took place across Britain to  honor veterans this anniversary would  have been commemorated with a huge  celebration but in the middle of a  pandemic that isn't possible millions of  people around the world including Second  World War veterans are isolating at home  but as Eric Swanson explains they came  up with new ways to mark the historic  day from nations that were brutally  attacked to those that were occupied to  the country that carries the burden for  starting at all the ceremonies to mark a  Victory in Europe day were as different  and somber as any in recent memory  Europeans not only stood silently they  stood alone Victory in Europe led to an  era of cooperation and trust for many  adversaries and yet the togetherness  that usually marks this day was missing  in Ottawa to the war memorial was a  stark backdrop for today's Remembrance  in this month of May 2020 let us  celebrate freedom and remain strong in  the face of adversity any of the happy  thousands who come to welcome peace the  celebrations we've come to take for  granted from the first jubilant events  when the Second World War ended to the  annual comrades in arms shoulder to  shoulder just weren't possible this year  they died to say we could live as free  people in a world of free nations they  risked all so our families and  neighborhoods could be safe they thought  I would make a good soldier norm Kirby  was just 17 when he became a good  soldier he was to attend the ceremonies  in Europe this year his image on the  poster commemorating the event still he  spoke recently about the importance of  the war he fought and survived in  Holland and we had quite a quite a  battle there and we lost lost a few guys  it was a war so devastating and  long-lasting that even in today's  challenging time it's hard to imagine  what they went through to walk beside a  guy knowing damn well that if he stepped  on the mine he would tell you he'd push  you out of the way he'd let the mind  blow up more than a million Canadians  and Newfoundlanders served in the war  more than 45,000 were killed they fought  and they died to defend the values that  we hold dear freedom peace and equality  and we are forever grateful  like many Canadians who liberated Europe  norm Kirby would never forget the  children whose future was changed on  this day seventy-five years ago it was  worth that worth it to see all of this  so don't ever think that it's a waste of  time it wasn't Eric Sorenson global news  and that is global national for this  Friday I'm Robin Gill we leave you  tonight with five notes that carry  infinite meaning horn players came  together while staying apart for the  last post it is played to honor the lost  the fallen and the dead thank you for  watching good night
 

